  "deviations": [
    "MMLU-Pro uses a 0-shot chain-of-thought prompt with the choices re-lettered A-J; the official 5-shot configuration is not used.",
    "LongBench v1 long-context rows are filtered to a 4K-32K reference-token window (4096 <= tokens <= 32768; no truncation) and are stratified by prompt length: 4k-8k 100 / 8k-16k 99 / 16k-32k 51. The whole 16K-32K pool is taken (narrativeqa 39 / qasper 3 / hotpotqa 9), so per-task quotas are no longer equal (the previous 63/63/62/62 split is retired).",
    "LongBench v1 rows are deduplicated by (task, input, context); upstream duplicate rows with different gold answers are merged and their answers unioned (narrativeqa: 18 rows merged).",
    "HotpotQA accuracy rows come from the distractor validation split, which is hard-only (level=hard for all 7,405 rows); they are converted into a single-request retrieval-agent task: the 10 distractor paragraphs live in meta and only the fixed search/lookup tool schemas are sent. The retrieval tools are not executed by the performance runner.",
    "Global-MMLU is scored generatively from option letters, not with lm-eval's likelihood-based scoring.",
    "Global-MMLU covers all 42 locally available languages x 100 rows, using a paired design: the same 100 sample_ids (chosen by subject round-robin from the 14,042 common ids) appear in every language, so cross-language differences compare translations of the same question.",
    "LiveCodeBench mixes two prompt types: function-level prompts for rows with starter code (LeetCode, functional hidden tests) and stdin/stdout prompts otherwise (AtCoder). code_pass1 must therefore support both testtype=functional and testtype=stdin rows; the window is release v5 + v6 (2024-09-22..2025-04-06).",
    "BFCL covers all 11 v4 single-turn categories (simple_python / simple_java / simple_javascript / multiple / parallel / parallel_multiple / irrelevance / live_simple / live_multiple / live_parallel / live_parallel_multiple); multi-turn categories are excluded. Category counts are 100/100/50/100/100/100/100/100/100/15/24 = 889 (pools smaller than the target contribute their whole pool; live_parallel 15, live_parallel_multiple 24). irrelevance has no upstream possible_answer file, so its gold is the empty answer list (meta.possible_answers = []) and rows are deduplicated by user question across all categories.",
    "search_agent excludes questions already selected by long_context/hotpotqa (cross-scenario duplication removed).",
    "Hidden LiveCodeBench tests are retained in full per row, except individual tests whose JSON exceeds the declared 256 KiB local-executor cap (meta.tests_dropped_large records them).",
    "Accuracy is data-only in this build: the set is not wired into the run (docs/TEST_PLAN.md is performance-only) and no evaluator/runner is implemented."
  ],
